<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marie-Adélaïde, Grand Duchess of Luxembourg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1894–1924</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marie-Adélaïde, Grand Duchess of Luxembourg, reigned from 1912 to 1919, succeeding her father William IV under the succession law he had changed in her favour. Her apparent sympathy for the German occupiers during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> and her interventions in politics made her unpopular, and in January 1919 she abdicated in favour of her sister Charlotte. She briefly entered a convent in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in 1924.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marie-adelaide-grand-duchess-of-luxembourg.jpg" alt="Marie-Adélaïde, Grand Duchess of Luxembourg" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bain News Service, publisher · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GD_Marie_Ad%C3%A9la%C3%AFde_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
